+## Privacy, not-for-profit stewardship and Responsible AI (2026-11-28)
+
+The owner requested privacy and Responsible AI on the main route. The new
+[official-source review](../../reference/regulatory/reviewed-updates/2026-11-28-privacy-residency-rai-review.md)
+and [research record](../../../.copilot-tracking/research/2026-11-28/capstone-privacy-residency-rai-research.md)
+support the wording. Not-for-profit status is owner-confirmed; charitable form
+and registered-provider applicability remain unknown. UK GDPR permits
+safeguarded transfers and does not impose a blanket UK-only rule.
+
+S01/S04 connect resident value and accountability to the mission. The demo
+labels constructed data, own-case access and retained human decisions. S11A
+names the proposed UK application/storage and Standard inference policy,
+without converting the retained Global/Sweden drawing into live residency
+proof. S15 names Responsible AI and a human reviewer with authority to change
+the outcome. S17 makes lawful purpose, minimisation, retention, rights and
+Legal/DPO real-data approval visible alongside the existing seven technical
+checks. B28 qualifies the unchanged public-cloud cost scenario and Global nano
+price; UK-only inference needs repricing.
+
+The complete 17-page main route remains 780 prepared seconds with a 110-second
+demo and 120-second reserve. Full local sovereignty remains in the separately
+confirmed six-minute appendix. The full deployment diagram is not shrunk or
+covered; only its native title changes. Historical notes, financial evidence,
+navigation and earlier review outcomes remain preserved.
+
+Before authoring, both new pitch regressions failed against the published
+delivery: not-for-profit stewardship was absent from the visible opening and
+the main narration lacked the qualified UK Standard target. Final generation,
+fit, package/link, parity and source-binding results are recorded below after
+execution. These tests concern presentation evidence, not privacy compliance.
+
+Validation tier: focused. Changes are presentation source, generated delivery,
+prose-only architecture/regulatory analysis and targeted document tests; no
+infrastructure, security control, permission, deployment, dependency or CI/gate
+semantics change. Legal/DPO, resident, professional, live privacy/RAI acceptance,
+rehearsal, projector and assistive-technology checks remain separate.
+
+Final local evidence: native Build/Verify/Render passed for all 56 pages.
+The first candidate wrapped the opening stewardship line beyond its measured
+frame; shortening that line preserved its meaning, font and geometry. The
+second candidate has zero warnings across 42 focused revised frames. Only
+pages 1, 13, 17, 21 and 56 changed pixels versus the published delivery; all six
+protected slide/note pairs are byte-identical for this increment. The 28 other
+source-revised and 179 inherited bound warnings remain historical limitations,
+not a fresh clean whole-deck claim.
+
+All 111 PDF jumps and hit regions were restored and read back; the changed
+pages passed text extraction. Sixteen pitch and ten preview tests passed under
+pytest, with three subtests. Native geometry, insertion, malformed-route,
+financial-refusal and four canonical source/delivery bindings passed. Ruff,
+format, whitespace and local links across seven source documents passed.
+The initial unittest preview import failure was corrected with the existing
+module import path; pytest collected all ten preview tests rather than silently
+omitting function-based tests. No new dependency or execution-policy change
+was needed. Independent exact-head review and actual hosted observations are
+recorded separately from these local results.
